{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01CzB3pC6ugif3tKsYRR33B9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Original framing fully stands. C1-C4 claims no adjustment needed.\n  Llama-70B confirms significant bias on both verbosity and formality, completing 3/3 independent architecture families\n  (GPT-4o proprietary US, Qwen3-32B open CN, Llama-70B open US) plus Claude negative control.\n  Double-rewrite placebo BT ≈ 50% eliminates Comparative Trap format amplification hypothesis entirely.\n  NLI gate ablation shows pass>fail directionally, cross-axis gradient is monotonic.\n  Four-layer MF1 defense complete: placebo BT + NLI gate + Claude control + cross-axis gradient.\n  SF3 (generalizability) fully resolved with 3rd judge. Reviewer path → 4.0 Conference.\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # CRITICAL PATH EXPERIMENTS\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Llama-3.3-70B verbosity — BT + GEE + Likert\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-021\"\n    description: >\n      Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct on 86 NLI-pass verbosity counterfactual pairs (LLMBar).\n      Pairwise dual-direction + Likert scoring. Reuses Qwen3-32B-rewritten pairs; rewriting and NLI independent of judge.\n    expected_results:\n      bt_p_verbose_wins: 0.75\n      bt_ci: [0.68, 0.82]\n      bt_p_value: 0.0001\n      bt_method: \"pair-level bootstrap (10000 iterations, seed=42)\"\n      n_pairs: 86\n      n_comparisons: 172\n      consistency_rate: 0.68\n      verbose_win_rate_sign: 0.847\n      sign_test_p: 0.00003\n      wilson_ci: [0.737, 0.918]\n      likert_ate: 0.065\n      likert_p: 0.45\n      likert_d: 0.058\n      likert_tie_rate: 0.59\n      gee_verbose_or: 11.5\n      gee_verbose_ci: [4.8, 27.6]\n      gee_verbose_p: 0.00001\n      gee_originality_or: 0.52\n      gee_originality_ci: [0.23, 1.18]\n      gee_originality_p: 0.115\n      direction_verbose_to_concise_orig_pref: 0.81\n      direction_verbose_to_concise_p: 0.0006\n      direction_concise_to_verbose_rewrite_pref: 0.88\n      direction_concise_to_verbose_p: 0.000005\n      blindspot_confirmed: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Llama-70B 经过 RLHF/DPO 训练，而人类标注者系统性偏好详细、结构化的回复——这是 RLHF 管线中的已知信号\n      （Dubois et al. 2024, Zheng et al. 2023）。GPT-4o (BT 76.0%) 和 Qwen3-32B (BT 77.3%)\n      已证明 verbosity bias 跨架构稳定。Llama 的训练语料（大量英文互联网数据）与 GPT-4o 高度重叠，\n      共享\"长=好\"偏见的来源相同。BT 0.75 位于 GPT-4o 和 Qwen 的中间偏低，反映 Llama 可能因\n      不同的 alignment 训练（Meta 的 RLHF 配方不同于 OpenAI/Alibaba）略有差异，但基本偏好方向一致。\n      GEE 分解中 style OR~11.5 与 GPT-4o (10.97) 和 Qwen (13.10) 高度一致，originality OR<1 NS\n      确认 verbosity 是 pure style bias。Likert p=0.45 落入衰减区：BT 75% 对应的效应量在 Likert\n      5/7/10-point scale 上被 tie rate ~59% 压缩殆尽，与已有的 7-method sensitivity table 模式完全吻合。\n      两个方向都偏好 verbose 内容证明不是 originality confound 而是真实的 style preference。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Llama-70B Verbosity Evidence Matrix\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\", \"CI/p\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"BT P(verbose)\", \"0.750\", \"[0.68, 0.82] p=0.0001\", \"Strong bias, 3rd arch family\"]\n          - [\"GEE Style OR\", \"11.50\", \"[4.8, 27.6] p<0.0001\", \"Pure style, consistent w/ GPT-4o/Qwen\"]\n          - [\"GEE Orig OR\", \"0.52\", \"[0.23, 1.18] p=0.115\", \"NS — confound-free\"]\n          - [\"Likert ATE\", \"+0.065\", \"p=0.45, d=0.058\", \"Blindspot confirmed\"]\n          - [\"Tie rate\", \"59%\", \"—\", \"Absorbs Likert signal\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: BT P(verbose) across 4 judges — GPT-4o 76.0%, Qwen3-32B 77.3%, Llama-70B 75.0%, Claude 54.1%. Error bars show bootstrap 95% CI. Dashed line at 50%.\"\n      - \"Forest plot: GEE Style OR (verbosity) across 3 target judges — GPT-4o 10.97, Qwen3-32B 13.10, Llama-70B 11.50. All significant. Claude OR=1.52 NS included as control.\"\n    analysis: >\n      3/3 target judges show verbosity BT 75-77% with pure style GEE profile (style OR 10-13, orig OR NS)。\n      Claude BT 54.1% NS 提供清晰的 negative control baseline。三个独立架构家族的一致性排除了\n      architecture-specific artifact 的可能性。Llama 的结果完善了 verbosity 作为\"clean style bias\"\n      轴的定位——C2 的 attenuation spectrum 在三个 judge 上完全复制。\n\n  - name: \"Llama-3.3-70B formality — BT + GEE + Likert\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-021\"\n    description: >\n      Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct on 88 NLI-pass formality counterfactual pairs (LLMBar).\n      Same setup as verbosity, dual-direction pairwise + Likert.\n    expected_results:\n      bt_p_formal_wins: 0.64\n      bt_ci: [0.58, 0.70]\n      bt_p_value: 0.003\n      bt_method: \"pair-level bootstrap (10000 iterations, seed=42)\"\n      n_pairs: 88\n      n_comparisons: 176\n      consistency_rate: 0.62\n      formal_win_rate_sign: 0.72\n      sign_test_p: 0.008\n      wilson_ci: [0.587, 0.823]\n      likert_ate: 0.035\n      likert_p: 0.55\n      likert_d: 0.028\n      likert_tie_rate: 0.65\n      gee_formal_or: 3.1\n      gee_formal_ci: [1.5, 6.4]\n      gee_formal_p: 0.002\n      gee_originality_or: 3.6\n      gee_originality_ci: [1.8, 7.2]\n      gee_originality_p: 0.0004\n      direction_formal_to_casual_win_rate: 0.78\n      direction_formal_to_casual_p: 0.002\n      direction_casual_to_formal_win_rate: 0.52\n      direction_casual_to_formal_p: 0.85\n      blindspot_confirmed: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Formality bias 在 GPT-4o (63.0%) 和 Qwen3-32B (66.5%) 上属于\"conditional style effect\"——\n      BT 显著但 GEE 同时检出 style 和 originality。Llama BT 0.64 位于两者中间，反映相同的混合机制：\n      formal→casual 方向上 original preference 与 style preference 叠加（78% win rate），\n      casual→formal 方向上两者抵消（52%）。这个方向不对称在三个 judge 上完全复制\n      （GPT-4o 78.8%/54.5%, Qwen 81.4%/50.0%, Llama 78%/52%），表明 originality confound\n      是 formality 轴的固有特征，不随 judge 变化。GEE style OR~3.1 落在 GPT-4o (2.21) 和 Qwen (4.20)\n      之间。Likert p=0.55 在衰减区，BT 64% 的效应量不足以穿透 65% tie rate 的 Likert ceiling。\n      Llama 确认 formality 的 stratified claim 地位不变：混合效应，非 pure style bias。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Formality BT Cross-Judge Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"BT\", \"95% CI\", \"p\", \"GEE Style OR\", \"GEE Orig OR\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"0.630\", \"[0.558, 0.703]\", \"<0.001\", \"2.21\", \"1.82\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B\", \"0.665\", \"[0.585, 0.739]\", \"<0.0001\", \"4.20\", \"4.70\"]\n          - [\"Llama-70B\", \"0.640\", \"[0.58, 0.70]\", \"0.003\", \"3.10\", \"3.60\"]\n          - [\"Claude (ctrl)\", \"0.562\", \"[0.489, 0.636]\", \"0.091\", \"1.47\", \"6.66\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-axis attenuation spectrum: 2×4 panel. Left column = BT, right column = Likert d. Rows = verbosity, formality. Each panel shows 4 judges. BT panels show clear bias; Likert panels all near zero.\"\n    analysis: >\n      三个 target judge 的 formality BT [0.63-0.665] 和 GEE profile (style+originality both sig)\n      高度一致。Direction asymmetry (formal→casual 78-81%, casual→formal 50-52%) 在三个 judge 上复制，\n      确认 C3 的 per-axis confound gradient 是 axis property 而非 judge artifact。\n      Llama 的加入使 formality 的\"conditional style effect\"定位从 2-judge 观察升格为 3-judge 规律。\n\n  - name: \"Double-rewrite placebo BT — formality (GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-022\"\n    description: >\n      Original text vs its double-rewrite (same style direction) for formality pairs.\n      Only rewriting artifact differs. BT on GPT-4o (API) + Qwen3-32B (local).\n      Data from double_rewrite_text field in verified_scaled_formality.jsonl.\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_placebo_bt: 0.51\n      gpt4o_placebo_ci: [0.44, 0.58]\n      gpt4o_placebo_p: 0.75\n      qwen32b_placebo_bt: 0.50\n      qwen32b_placebo_ci: [0.43, 0.57]\n      qwen32b_placebo_p: 0.92\n      n_pairs_formality: 88\n      n_comparisons: 176\n      gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.50\n      qwen32b_formal_win_rate: 0.49\n    result_rationale: >\n      Placebo 对 (original vs double-rewrite) 中两个文本具有相同的 style 方向（都是 formal 或都是 casual），\n      唯一差异是 rewriting 过程引入的表面变异（词汇选择、句法微调）。在 best 档位，BT ≈ 50% 的原因是：\n      (1) rewriting artifacts 在两次独立 rewrite 之间是随机的，不构成系统性 preference；\n      (2) Qwen3-32B rewriter 的 double-rewrite 保持了 style 和 content 的一致性（NLI 通过率已验证）；\n      (3) 评委没有理由系统性偏好 original 或 double-rewrite，因为两者风格相同、质量相当。\n      这直接证伪了 Jeong et al. (2025) Comparative Trap 担忧的核心：pairwise format 本身不制造 bias。\n      当 style 差异不存在时，BT = chance；当 style 差异存在时（treatment pairs），BT >> 50%。\n      因此 treatment BT 中的超额信号完全来自 style manipulation，而非 format amplification。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Placebo BT vs Treatment BT — Formality\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"Treatment BT\", \"Placebo BT\", \"Δ\", \"Placebo p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"0.630\", \"0.510\", \"-0.120\", \"0.75\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B\", \"0.665\", \"0.500\", \"-0.165\", \"0.92\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired dot plot: Treatment BT vs Placebo BT for each judge × axis. Treatment dots clearly above 50% line, placebo dots clustered at 50%. Horizontal reference line at 0.50.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Placebo BT 在两个 judge 上都不显著偏离 50%，CI 宽约 14pp 反映 n=88 的统计功率有限但足以排除\n      大效应。Treatment-Placebo gap (12-16.5pp) 证明 observed BT 信号来自 style manipulation\n      而非 rewriting format。这是 MF1 最强防御：从 \"bounded amplification risk\" 升级为\n      \"format amplification empirically excluded\"。\n\n  - name: \"Double-rewrite placebo BT — verbosity (GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-022\"\n    description: >\n      Same placebo design for verbosity pairs. Data from double_rewrite_text in verified_verbosity.jsonl.\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_placebo_bt: 0.52\n      gpt4o_placebo_ci: [0.45, 0.59]\n      gpt4o_placebo_p: 0.60\n      qwen32b_placebo_bt: 0.51\n      qwen32b_placebo_ci: [0.44, 0.58]\n      qwen32b_placebo_p: 0.78\n      n_pairs_verbosity: 86\n      n_comparisons: 172\n    result_rationale: >\n      Verbosity placebo BT 预期略高于 formality (0.51-0.52 vs 0.50-0.51)，因为 verbosity\n      rewriting 涉及更大的文本变化（direction-aware NLI rejection 14% vs formality 12%），\n      double-rewrite 之间的随机变异也稍大。但仍然不显著偏离 50%，确认 rewriting noise\n      不构成系统性 preference。Treatment BT (76-77%) vs Placebo BT (51-52%) 的 gap 为 24-26pp，\n      是 formality gap (12-16pp) 的近两倍——这与 verbosity 作为 stronger true bias 的定位一致。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Placebo BT vs Treatment BT — Verbosity\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"Treatment BT\", \"Placebo BT\", \"Δ\", \"Placebo p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"0.760\", \"0.520\", \"-0.240\", \"0.60\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B\", \"0.773\", \"0.510\", \"-0.263\", \"0.78\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Combined figure (formality + verbosity): 4 judge×axis cells, each cell shows Treatment BT (filled circle) and Placebo BT (open circle) with 95% CI. Clear separation in all treatment cells, placebo cells overlap 50% line.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Verbosity 的 treatment-placebo gap 是 formality 的近两倍 (24-26pp vs 12-16pp)，\n      与 pure style bias vs conditional style effect 的分类完全一致。Placebo BT 在两个轴上都 ≈ 50%，\n      排除了\"某些轴的 amplification 比其他轴更强\"的 reviewer 反驳——format amplification\n      在所有轴上都是 null。\n\n  - name: \"NLI gate ablation — BT on pass vs fail vs all\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-023\"\n    description: >\n      Bounding analysis: compute BT separately on NLI-pass pairs, NLI-fail pairs, and all pairs\n      for formality and verbosity. Quantifies content-mediated signal proportion.\n    expected_results:\n      formality_nli_pass_bt: 0.665\n      formality_nli_pass_n: 88\n      formality_nli_fail_bt: 0.57\n      formality_nli_fail_n: 12\n      formality_all_bt: 0.609\n      formality_all_n: 100\n      formality_pass_minus_fail_pp: 9.5\n      verbosity_nli_pass_bt: 0.773\n      verbosity_nli_pass_n: 86\n      verbosity_nli_fail_bt: 0.66\n      verbosity_nli_fail_n: 14\n      verbosity_all_bt: 0.753\n      verbosity_all_n: 100\n      verbosity_pass_minus_fail_pp: 11.3\n      note: \"NLI-fail n too small for individual significance; reported as bounds\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      NLI-pass pairs 的 BT 应等于已知的 canonical 值（formality 66.5%, verbosity 77.3%）。\n      NLI-fail pairs 的 BT 预期更低，原因是：(1) NLI-fail 意味着 rewriting 改变了内容，\n      content quality 变化可能与 style 方向不一致，稀释了 style-only signal；\n      (2) NLI FN selection bias 分析已证明 gate 是 conservative（fail pairs 有更大的 style 变化，\n      BLEU d=-0.46, TF-IDF d=-0.62），这些更激进的 rewrite 同时引入了更多 content 噪声。\n      Pass-fail difference 10-12pp 位于 best 档位 [5, 20] 的中段，表明 NLI gate 有效地\n      去除了约 10pp 的 content-mediated signal。Verbosity 的 pass-fail gap (11.3pp) 略大于\n      formality (9.5pp)，因为 verbosity rewriting 更 invasive（14% fail vs 12%），\n      content 污染程度更高。All-pairs BT 介于 pass 和 fail 之间，权重向 pass 倾斜\n      （因为 pass 占 85-88%）。这个 bounding analysis 不声称因果关系（n_fail 太小），\n      但方向一致性支持 NLI gate 的 design rationale：gate removes content-mediated component。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"NLI Gate Ablation: BT by Gate Status\"\n        columns: [\"Axis\", \"NLI-pass BT (n)\", \"NLI-fail BT (n)\", \"All BT (n)\", \"Δ(pass-fail) pp\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Formality\", \"0.665 (88)\", \"0.570 (12)\", \"0.609 (100)\", \"+9.5\"]\n          - [\"Verbosity\", \"0.773 (86)\", \"0.660 (14)\", \"0.753 (100)\", \"+11.3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: BT by NLI gate status (pass/fail/all) × axis. Error bars for pass group from bootstrap; fail group too small for reliable CI, shown with wide whiskers. Annotation: 'n=12' and 'n=14' above fail bars.\"\n    analysis: >\n      NLI-pass BT 始终高于 NLI-fail BT，方向一致。这表明 gate 成功隔离了 style-only signal\n      从 style+content 混合信号中。Gate 效果在两个轴上均为 ~10pp，可解释性清晰。\n      NLI-fail 的非零 BT (>50%) 表明即使 content 发生变化，style preference 仍然存在但被稀释——\n      这与\"NLI gate removes content-mediated amplification\"的叙事一致。\n      结合 placebo BT ≈ 50%，NLI ablation 提供了 MF1 防御的第三层证据。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-axis gradient formalization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-024\"\n    description: >\n      Compute NLI rejection rate (manipulation invasiveness proxy) vs BT for 3 axes.\n      Qualitative 3-point anti-amplification argument.\n    expected_results:\n      register_nli_rejection: 0.06\n      register_bt_qwen: 0.553\n      register_bt_gpt4o: 0.570\n      formality_nli_rejection: 0.12\n      formality_bt_qwen: 0.665\n      formality_bt_gpt4o: 0.630\n      verbosity_nli_rejection: 0.14\n      verbosity_bt_qwen: 0.773\n      verbosity_bt_gpt4o: 0.760\n      gradient_monotonic: true\n      spearman_rho: 1.0\n      note: \"3 points only — qualitative argument, not statistical test\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      三个轴的 NLI rejection rate 从低到高：register (6%) < formality (12%) < verbosity (14%)。\n      BT 从低到高：register (55%) < formality (63-67%) < verbosity (76-77%)。两者严格单调。\n      Anti-amplification 的核心论点：如果 format amplification 是 BT 升高的原因，\n      那么 amplification 幅度应与 manipulation invasiveness 无关或呈简单正比关系。\n      但实际观察到的 per-axis BT 变异跨越 20+ pp (55% → 77%)，而 NLI rejection 仅变化 8pp (6% → 14%)。\n      更重要的是，placebo BT ≈ 50% 已直接证明 format 本身不产生 amplification，\n      因此这里的 gradient 反映的是 three axes have genuinely different bias levels in the judges，\n      而非 amplification 的 differential。Register 的弱 BT 对应低 style bias（originality dominant）；\n      verbosity 的强 BT 对应 pure style bias。这个 gradient 是 per-axis claim stratification (C2/C3)\n      的可视化证据，同时作为 MF1 防御的补充（非主力）论据。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Axis Gradient: NLI Rejection Rate vs BT\"\n        columns: [\"Axis\", \"NLI Rejection %\", \"Qwen BT\", \"GPT-4o BT\", \"GEE Style/Orig Ratio\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Register\", \"6%\", \"0.553\", \"0.570\", \"0.33 (orig dominant)\"]\n          - [\"Formality\", \"12%\", \"0.665\", \"0.630\", \"0.89–1.91 (mixed)\"]\n          - [\"Verbosity\", \"14%\", \"0.773\", \"0.760\", \"22–27 (style dominant)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: x-axis = NLI rejection rate (%), y-axis = BT. Two series (GPT-4o diamonds, Qwen3-32B circles). Three points each, both monotonically increasing. Dashed line at BT=0.50. Labels on each point: axis name.\"\n    analysis: >\n      单调梯度在两个 judge 上独立复制 (Spearman ρ=1.0 for both)，排除了 judge-specific artifact。\n      结合 placebo BT ≈ 50%，gradient 的解释是明确的：per-axis BT 差异来自 genuine bias level 差异，\n      不来自 differential amplification。3 点仅支持 qualitative argument，不做统计推断。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # SECONDARY / SUPERSEDED EXPERIMENTS\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise (Gemini-2.0-Flash)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      Gemini-2.0-Flash as additional judge on 100 formality counterfactual pairs (LLMBar).\n      Claude Sonnet already completed as negative control (BT 56.2% NS).\n      Remaining: Gemini-2.0-Flash.\n    expected_results:\n      gemini_bt: 0.62\n      gemini_ci: [0.54, 0.70]\n      gemini_p: 0.008\n      gemini_likert_ate: 0.04\n      gemini_likert_p: 0.60\n      gemini_gee_style_or: 2.8\n      gemini_gee_orig_or: 3.2\n      gemini_consistency_rate: 0.58\n      blindspot_confirmed: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Gemini-2.0-Flash 是 Google 的轻量级指令模型，训练目标同样包含 RLHF。\n      Flash 模型通常表现出与更大模型类似但稍弱的 style preference，\n      因为其参数容量有限导致风格判断的 resolution 较低。BT 0.62 略低于 GPT-4o (0.63)\n      和 Qwen (0.665)，符合 lightweight model = weaker but present bias 的预期。\n      GEE decomposition 会显示与 GPT-4o 类似的 mixed confound 结构（style + originality both sig）。\n      在 best 档位，Gemini 提供了第 4 个 architecture family 的确认，但主要贡献已被 Llama 覆盖。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Expanded Evidence Matrix Table (4 target judges + 1 control) showing BT, Likert p, GEE decomposition\"\n    analysis: >\n      Gemini 的加入使 generalizability 从 3 → 4 families，但边际价值有限。\n      在 best 档位的叙事中，Gemini 是 robustness row 而非 headline result。\n      SF3 已被 Llama 解决，Gemini 是 bonus。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality (Qwen3-32B + Claude on AlpacaEval/MT-Bench)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      Extend cross-benchmark coverage. GPT-4o results already exist for AlpacaEval (BT 72.7%)\n      and MT-Bench (BT 69.2%). Run Qwen3-32B and Claude on same benchmark CFs.\n    expected_results:\n      qwen_alpacaeval_bt: 0.68\n      qwen_alpacaeval_p: 0.0001\n      qwen_mtbench_bt: 0.72\n      qwen_mtbench_p: 0.0001\n      claude_alpacaeval_bt: 0.54\n      claude_alpacaeval_p: 0.30\n      claude_mtbench_bt: 0.53\n      claude_mtbench_p: 0.45\n      cross_benchmark_consistency: \"3/3 benchmarks show bias for target judges, 0/3 for Claude\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Qwen3-32B 在 LLMBar formality 上 BT=66.5%，其 AlpacaEval/MT-Bench 值预期与 GPT-4o 的\n      cross-benchmark pattern 平行。AlpacaEval 的 formality bias 通常较强\n      （GPT-4o 72.7% > LLMBar 63.0%），因为 AlpacaEval 的开放式问题给 style 更多影响空间。\n      MT-Bench 的结构化多轮格式对 formality 更敏感。\n      Claude 在所有 benchmark 上预期 NS，维持 negative control 一致性。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Benchmark Formality BT Matrix\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"GPT-4o\", \"Qwen3-32B\", \"Claude\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LLMBar\", \"0.630\", \"0.665\", \"0.562 NS\"]\n          - [\"AlpacaEval\", \"0.727\", \"0.680\", \"0.540 NS\"]\n          - [\"MT-Bench\", \"0.692\", \"0.720\", \"0.530 NS\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-benchmark 一致性为 C1 method claim 提供外部效度。\n      3 benchmarks × 2 target judges 全部显著、Claude 全部 NS 的 6×1 pattern\n      使\"CSD pipeline detects bias in biased judges, not in unbiased ones\"的 claim 不可争辩。\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis (systematic)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      Systematic comparison of Likert ATE and pairwise BT across all judge × benchmark × axis cells.\n      Quantifies attenuation spectrum.\n    expected_results:\n      n_cells_total: 18\n      n_cells_bt_significant: 12\n      n_cells_likert_significant: 2\n      n_blindspot_cells: 10\n      attenuation_threshold_bt: 0.80\n      note: \"Likert detects only when BT > 80% (e.g., AlpacaEval verbosity Qwen BT=84.1%)\"\n      sensitivity_ratio: \"BT 6× more sensitive than Likert (12/18 vs 2/18 significant cells)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有数据中，Likert 仅在两个 cell 显著：(1) MT-Bench formality GPT-4o (p=0.016, d=0.167, BT 69.2%)\n      和 (2) AlpacaEval verbosity Qwen3-32B (p=0.0003, d=0.375, BT 84.1%)。\n      所有其他 BT 显著的 cell (formality LLMBar GPT-4o/Qwen/Llama, verbosity LLMBar 全部, etc.)\n      的 Likert p > 0.15。这定义了 attenuation spectrum 的 empirical boundary：\n      BT ~80% 是 Likert 检出的 threshold，BT 60-77% 完全在 Likert blindspot 中。\n      Systematic analysis 将这些散点整合为 C2 的定量 claim：\n      \"Pairwise BT is 6× more sensitive than Likert for detecting style bias in LLM judges。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Detection Matrix: BT sig vs Likert sig\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"Likert sig\", \"Likert NS\", \"Total\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"BT sig\", \"2 (MT-B form, AE verb)\", \"10 (Blindspot)\", \"12\"]\n          - [\"BT NS\", \"0\", \"6 (true null)\", \"6\"]\n          - [\"Total\", \"2\", \"16\", \"18\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: x-axis = BT win probability, y-axis = Likert Cohen's d. Each point is a judge×benchmark×axis cell. Points colored by significance. Vertical dashed line at BT=0.80. Horizontal dashed line at d=0.20. The Blindspot quadrant (BT>0.50, d<0.20) contains 10/12 significant BT cells.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Systematic 2×2 detection matrix 是 C2 Likert Blindspot 最直接的证据。\n      10/12 BT-significant cells 的 Likert 检测失败定义了\"measurement attenuation spectrum\"的实证边界。\n\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite, all cells)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Extend original vs double-rewrite pairwise to all judge × benchmark combinations.\n      Quantifies original preference confound.\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_llmbar_placebo_bt: 0.51\n      qwen32b_llmbar_placebo_bt: 0.50\n      llama70b_llmbar_placebo_bt: 0.52\n      cross_judge_placebo_range: [0.48, 0.53]\n      all_p_nonsignificant: true\n      original_preference_absent: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      与 exp-022 共享 rationale。当 style 操纵不存在时，评委对 original vs double-rewrite\n      没有系统性偏好。Llama-70B 的 placebo BT 0.52 略高反映其作为 open model 可能\n      对 text 微小差异更敏感，但仍不显著。Cross-judge 的 [0.48, 0.53] range 确认\n      original preference confound 在所有 judge 上都不存在。\n      这解决了 exp-005 描述中 DREAM 提到的跨 judge 泛化性问题。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      与 exp-022 互补。exp-005 侧重 original preference confound 的量化，\n      exp-022 侧重 format amplification 的排除。Best 档位下两者都是 BT ≈ 50%，\n      提供同一 null result 的双重解读。\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control (Llama-3.1-70B as rewriter)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      Replace Qwen3-32B rewriter with Llama-3.1-70B for counterfactual generation.\n      Compare NLI pass rate and formality pairwise BT with Qwen3-32B baseline.\n    expected_results:\n      llama_rewriter_nli_pass_rate: 0.87\n      llama_rewriter_bt: 0.65\n      llama_rewriter_ci: [0.57, 0.73]\n      llama_rewriter_p: 0.002\n      vs_qwen_bt_delta_pp: -1.5\n      vs_qwen_ci_overlap: true\n      vs_gpt4o_rewriter_bt: 0.644\n      three_rewriter_range: [0.644, 0.665]\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有两个 rewriter 的数据：Qwen3-32B (BT 66.5%) 和 GPT-4o (BT 64.4%)，CIs 重叠。\n      第三个 rewriter (Llama) 预期产生 BT 65%，落在 [64.4, 66.5] 范围内。\n      NLI pass rate 0.87 与 Qwen (0.88) 和 GPT-4o (0.90) 相近，反映 NLI 验证\n      对 rewriter 选择不敏感——因为 NLI 判断的是 content 保持度，不是 rewriting 风格。\n      三个 rewriter 的 BT 范围 <2.1pp 强力证明 CSD pipeline 的 rewriter-independence，\n      消除了\"observed bias is Qwen-specific rewriting artifact\"的审稿人 concern。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Rewriter Independence Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"Rewriter\", \"NLI Pass %\", \"Formality BT\", \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B (primary)\", \"88%\", \"0.665\", \"[0.585, 0.739]\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"90%\", \"0.644\", \"[0.561, 0.728]\"]\n          - [\"Llama-3.1-70B\", \"87%\", \"0.650\", \"[0.57, 0.73]\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      三个 rewriter 确认 pipeline 的 rewriter-independent 性质。BT range < 2.1pp\n      远小于 treatment effect (15-17pp over 50% baseline)。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # DONE IN REGISTRY (plan status outdated)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Scaled replication (n=400 formality)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      NOTE: Registry shows exp-006 DONE (n=400, BT 67.5% [63.7, 71.3]).\n      Plan status outdated. Predictions match actuals.\n    expected_results:\n      actual_n: 400\n      actual_nli_pass: 355\n      actual_bt: 0.675\n      actual_ci: [0.637, 0.713]\n      actual_ci_width_pp: 7.6\n      actual_p: 0.0001\n      actual_likert_ate: -0.059\n      actual_likert_p: 0.5999\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成。n=400 使 CI 从 15.4pp 缩窄至 7.6pp (2× improvement)。\n      BT 67.5% vs n=100 的 66.5% 仅差 +1.0pp，确认 effect stability。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Completed. Confirms effect stability at scale.\"\n\n  - name: \"GPT-4o verbosity + register scoring\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-020\"\n    description: >\n      NOTE: Registry shows gpt4o_verbosity (BT 76.0%) and gpt4o_register (BT 57.0%) both DONE.\n      Plan status outdated.\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt: 0.760\n      gpt4o_verbosity_likert_p: 0.4033\n      gpt4o_register_bt: 0.570\n      gpt4o_register_likert_p: 0.7849\n    result_rationale: \"已完成。数据在 registry 中。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Completed. Both axes confirmed as expected.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":278,"cache_read_input_tokens":41882,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":278},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"12047068-2416-4fe3-bb04-14e003f3607a","uuid":"03ebc961-7b60-4fd3-889e-1fcf906f7070"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":394307,"duration_api_ms":396097,"num_turns":4,"result":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Original framing fully stands. C1-C4 claims no adjustment needed.\n  Llama-70B confirms significant bias on both verbosity and formality, completing 3/3 independent architecture families\n  (GPT-4o proprietary US, Qwen3-32B open CN, Llama-70B open US) plus Claude negative control.\n  Double-rewrite placebo BT ≈ 50% eliminates Comparative Trap format amplification hypothesis entirely.\n  NLI gate ablation shows pass>fail directionally, cross-axis gradient is monotonic.\n  Four-layer MF1 defense complete: placebo BT + NLI gate + Claude control + cross-axis gradient.\n  SF3 (generalizability) fully resolved with 3rd judge. Reviewer path → 4.0 Conference.\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # CRITICAL PATH EXPERIMENTS\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Llama-3.3-70B verbosity — BT + GEE + Likert\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-021\"\n    description: >\n      Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct on 86 NLI-pass verbosity counterfactual pairs (LLMBar).\n      Pairwise dual-direction + Likert scoring. Reuses Qwen3-32B-rewritten pairs; rewriting and NLI independent of judge.\n    expected_results:\n      bt_p_verbose_wins: 0.75\n      bt_ci: [0.68, 0.82]\n      bt_p_value: 0.0001\n      bt_method: \"pair-level bootstrap (10000 iterations, seed=42)\"\n      n_pairs: 86\n      n_comparisons: 172\n      consistency_rate: 0.68\n      verbose_win_rate_sign: 0.847\n      sign_test_p: 0.00003\n      wilson_ci: [0.737, 0.918]\n      likert_ate: 0.065\n      likert_p: 0.45\n      likert_d: 0.058\n      likert_tie_rate: 0.59\n      gee_verbose_or: 11.5\n      gee_verbose_ci: [4.8, 27.6]\n      gee_verbose_p: 0.00001\n      gee_originality_or: 0.52\n      gee_originality_ci: [0.23, 1.18]\n      gee_originality_p: 0.115\n      direction_verbose_to_concise_orig_pref: 0.81\n      direction_verbose_to_concise_p: 0.0006\n      direction_concise_to_verbose_rewrite_pref: 0.88\n      direction_concise_to_verbose_p: 0.000005\n      blindspot_confirmed: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Llama-70B 经过 RLHF/DPO 训练，而人类标注者系统性偏好详细、结构化的回复——这是 RLHF 管线中的已知信号\n      （Dubois et al. 2024, Zheng et al. 2023）。GPT-4o (BT 76.0%) 和 Qwen3-32B (BT 77.3%)\n      已证明 verbosity bias 跨架构稳定。Llama 的训练语料（大量英文互联网数据）与 GPT-4o 高度重叠，\n      共享\"长=好\"偏见的来源相同。BT 0.75 位于 GPT-4o 和 Qwen 的中间偏低，反映 Llama 可能因\n      不同的 alignment 训练（Meta 的 RLHF 配方不同于 OpenAI/Alibaba）略有差异，但基本偏好方向一致。\n      GEE 分解中 style OR~11.5 与 GPT-4o (10.97) 和 Qwen (13.10) 高度一致，originality OR<1 NS\n      确认 verbosity 是 pure style bias。Likert p=0.45 落入衰减区：BT 75% 对应的效应量在 Likert\n      5/7/10-point scale 上被 tie rate ~59% 压缩殆尽，与已有的 7-method sensitivity table 模式完全吻合。\n      两个方向都偏好 verbose 内容证明不是 originality confound 而是真实的 style preference。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Llama-70B Verbosity Evidence Matrix\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\", \"CI/p\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"BT P(verbose)\", \"0.750\", \"[0.68, 0.82] p=0.0001\", \"Strong bias, 3rd arch family\"]\n          - [\"GEE Style OR\", \"11.50\", \"[4.8, 27.6] p<0.0001\", \"Pure style, consistent w/ GPT-4o/Qwen\"]\n          - [\"GEE Orig OR\", \"0.52\", \"[0.23, 1.18] p=0.115\", \"NS — confound-free\"]\n          - [\"Likert ATE\", \"+0.065\", \"p=0.45, d=0.058\", \"Blindspot confirmed\"]\n          - [\"Tie rate\", \"59%\", \"—\", \"Absorbs Likert signal\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: BT P(verbose) across 4 judges — GPT-4o 76.0%, Qwen3-32B 77.3%, Llama-70B 75.0%, Claude 54.1%. Error bars show bootstrap 95% CI. Dashed line at 50%.\"\n      - \"Forest plot: GEE Style OR (verbosity) across 3 target judges — GPT-4o 10.97, Qwen3-32B 13.10, Llama-70B 11.50. All significant. Claude OR=1.52 NS included as control.\"\n    analysis: >\n      3/3 target judges show verbosity BT 75-77% with pure style GEE profile (style OR 10-13, orig OR NS)。\n      Claude BT 54.1% NS 提供清晰的 negative control baseline。三个独立架构家族的一致性排除了\n      architecture-specific artifact 的可能性。Llama 的结果完善了 verbosity 作为\"clean style bias\"\n      轴的定位——C2 的 attenuation spectrum 在三个 judge 上完全复制。\n\n  - name: \"Llama-3.3-70B formality — BT + GEE + Likert\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-021\"\n    description: >\n      Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct on 88 NLI-pass formality counterfactual pairs (LLMBar).\n      Same setup as verbosity, dual-direction pairwise + Likert.\n    expected_results:\n      bt_p_formal_wins: 0.64\n      bt_ci: [0.58, 0.70]\n      bt_p_value: 0.003\n      bt_method: \"pair-level bootstrap (10000 iterations, seed=42)\"\n      n_pairs: 88\n      n_comparisons: 176\n      consistency_rate: 0.62\n      formal_win_rate_sign: 0.72\n      sign_test_p: 0.008\n      wilson_ci: [0.587, 0.823]\n      likert_ate: 0.035\n      likert_p: 0.55\n      likert_d: 0.028\n      likert_tie_rate: 0.65\n      gee_formal_or: 3.1\n      gee_formal_ci: [1.5, 6.4]\n      gee_formal_p: 0.002\n      gee_originality_or: 3.6\n      gee_originality_ci: [1.8, 7.2]\n      gee_originality_p: 0.0004\n      direction_formal_to_casual_win_rate: 0.78\n      direction_formal_to_casual_p: 0.002\n      direction_casual_to_formal_win_rate: 0.52\n      direction_casual_to_formal_p: 0.85\n      blindspot_confirmed: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Formality bias 在 GPT-4o (63.0%) 和 Qwen3-32B (66.5%) 上属于\"conditional style effect\"——\n      BT 显著但 GEE 同时检出 style 和 originality。Llama BT 0.64 位于两者中间，反映相同的混合机制：\n      formal→casual 方向上 original preference 与 style preference 叠加（78% win rate），\n      casual→formal 方向上两者抵消（52%）。这个方向不对称在三个 judge 上完全复制\n      （GPT-4o 78.8%/54.5%, Qwen 81.4%/50.0%, Llama 78%/52%），表明 originality confound\n      是 formality 轴的固有特征，不随 judge 变化。GEE style OR~3.1 落在 GPT-4o (2.21) 和 Qwen (4.20)\n      之间。Likert p=0.55 在衰减区，BT 64% 的效应量不足以穿透 65% tie rate 的 Likert ceiling。\n      Llama 确认 formality 的 stratified claim 地位不变：混合效应，非 pure style bias。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Formality BT Cross-Judge Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"BT\", \"95% CI\", \"p\", \"GEE Style OR\", \"GEE Orig OR\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"0.630\", \"[0.558, 0.703]\", \"<0.001\", \"2.21\", \"1.82\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B\", \"0.665\", \"[0.585, 0.739]\", \"<0.0001\", \"4.20\", \"4.70\"]\n          - [\"Llama-70B\", \"0.640\", \"[0.58, 0.70]\", \"0.003\", \"3.10\", \"3.60\"]\n          - [\"Claude (ctrl)\", \"0.562\", \"[0.489, 0.636]\", \"0.091\", \"1.47\", \"6.66\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-axis attenuation spectrum: 2×4 panel. Left column = BT, right column = Likert d. Rows = verbosity, formality. Each panel shows 4 judges. BT panels show clear bias; Likert panels all near zero.\"\n    analysis: >\n      三个 target judge 的 formality BT [0.63-0.665] 和 GEE profile (style+originality both sig)\n      高度一致。Direction asymmetry (formal→casual 78-81%, casual→formal 50-52%) 在三个 judge 上复制，\n      确认 C3 的 per-axis confound gradient 是 axis property 而非 judge artifact。\n      Llama 的加入使 formality 的\"conditional style effect\"定位从 2-judge 观察升格为 3-judge 规律。\n\n  - name: \"Double-rewrite placebo BT — formality (GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-022\"\n    description: >\n      Original text vs its double-rewrite (same style direction) for formality pairs.\n      Only rewriting artifact differs. BT on GPT-4o (API) + Qwen3-32B (local).\n      Data from double_rewrite_text field in verified_scaled_formality.jsonl.\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_placebo_bt: 0.51\n      gpt4o_placebo_ci: [0.44, 0.58]\n      gpt4o_placebo_p: 0.75\n      qwen32b_placebo_bt: 0.50\n      qwen32b_placebo_ci: [0.43, 0.57]\n      qwen32b_placebo_p: 0.92\n      n_pairs_formality: 88\n      n_comparisons: 176\n      gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.50\n      qwen32b_formal_win_rate: 0.49\n    result_rationale: >\n      Placebo 对 (original vs double-rewrite) 中两个文本具有相同的 style 方向（都是 formal 或都是 casual），\n      唯一差异是 rewriting 过程引入的表面变异（词汇选择、句法微调）。在 best 档位，BT ≈ 50% 的原因是：\n      (1) rewriting artifacts 在两次独立 rewrite 之间是随机的，不构成系统性 preference；\n      (2) Qwen3-32B rewriter 的 double-rewrite 保持了 style 和 content 的一致性（NLI 通过率已验证）；\n      (3) 评委没有理由系统性偏好 original 或 double-rewrite，因为两者风格相同、质量相当。\n      这直接证伪了 Jeong et al. (2025) Comparative Trap 担忧的核心：pairwise format 本身不制造 bias。\n      当 style 差异不存在时，BT = chance；当 style 差异存在时（treatment pairs），BT >> 50%。\n      因此 treatment BT 中的超额信号完全来自 style manipulation，而非 format amplification。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Placebo BT vs Treatment BT — Formality\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"Treatment BT\", \"Placebo BT\", \"Δ\", \"Placebo p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"0.630\", \"0.510\", \"-0.120\", \"0.75\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B\", \"0.665\", \"0.500\", \"-0.165\", \"0.92\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired dot plot: Treatment BT vs Placebo BT for each judge × axis. Treatment dots clearly above 50% line, placebo dots clustered at 50%. Horizontal reference line at 0.50.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Placebo BT 在两个 judge 上都不显著偏离 50%，CI 宽约 14pp 反映 n=88 的统计功率有限但足以排除\n      大效应。Treatment-Placebo gap (12-16.5pp) 证明 observed BT 信号来自 style manipulation\n      而非 rewriting format。这是 MF1 最强防御：从 \"bounded amplification risk\" 升级为\n      \"format amplification empirically excluded\"。\n\n  - name: \"Double-rewrite placebo BT — verbosity (GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-022\"\n    description: >\n      Same placebo design for verbosity pairs. Data from double_rewrite_text in verified_verbosity.jsonl.\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_placebo_bt: 0.52\n      gpt4o_placebo_ci: [0.45, 0.59]\n      gpt4o_placebo_p: 0.60\n      qwen32b_placebo_bt: 0.51\n      qwen32b_placebo_ci: [0.44, 0.58]\n      qwen32b_placebo_p: 0.78\n      n_pairs_verbosity: 86\n      n_comparisons: 172\n    result_rationale: >\n      Verbosity placebo BT 预期略高于 formality (0.51-0.52 vs 0.50-0.51)，因为 verbosity\n      rewriting 涉及更大的文本变化（direction-aware NLI rejection 14% vs formality 12%），\n      double-rewrite 之间的随机变异也稍大。但仍然不显著偏离 50%，确认 rewriting noise\n      不构成系统性 preference。Treatment BT (76-77%) vs Placebo BT (51-52%) 的 gap 为 24-26pp，\n      是 formality gap (12-16pp) 的近两倍——这与 verbosity 作为 stronger true bias 的定位一致。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Placebo BT vs Treatment BT — Verbosity\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"Treatment BT\", \"Placebo BT\", \"Δ\", \"Placebo p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"0.760\", \"0.520\", \"-0.240\", \"0.60\"]\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B\", \"0.773\", \"0.510\", \"-0.263\", \"0.78\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Combined figure (formality + verbosity): 4 judge×axis cells, each cell shows Treatment BT (filled circle) and Placebo BT (open circle) with 95% CI. Clear separation in all treatment cells, placebo cells overlap 50% line.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Verbosity 的 treatment-placebo gap 是 formality 的近两倍 (24-26pp vs 12-16pp)，\n      与 pure style bias vs conditional style effect 的分类完全一致。Placebo BT 在两个轴上都 ≈ 50%，\n      排除了\"某些轴的 amplification 比其他轴更强\"的 reviewer 反驳——format amplification\n      在所有轴上都是 null。\n\n  - name: \"NLI gate ablation — BT on pass vs fail vs all\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-023\"\n    description: >\n      Bounding analysis: compute BT separately on NLI-pass pairs, NLI-fail pairs, and all pairs\n      for formality and verbosity. Quantifies content-mediated signal proportion.\n    expected_results:\n      formality_nli_pass_bt: 0.665\n      formality_nli_pass_n: 88\n      formality_nli_fail_bt: 0.57\n      formality_nli_fail_n: 12\n      formality_all_bt: 0.609\n      formality_all_n: 100\n      formality_pass_minus_fail_pp: 9.5\n      verbosity_nli_pass_bt: 0.773\n      verbosity_nli_pass_n: 86\n      verbosity_nli_fail_bt: 0.66\n      verbosity_nli_fail_n: 14\n      verbosity_all_bt: 0.753\n      verbosity_all_n: 100\n      verbosity_pass_minus_fail_pp: 11.3\n      note: \"NLI-fail n too small for individual significance; reported as bounds\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      NLI-pass pairs 的 BT 应等于已知的 canonical 值（formality 66.5%, verbosity 77.3%）。\n      NLI-fail pairs 的 BT 预期更低，原因是：(1) NLI-fail 意味着 rewriting 改变了内容，\n      content quality 变化可能与 style 方向不一致，稀释了 style-only signal；\n      (2) NLI FN selection bias 分析已证明 gate 是 conservative（fail pairs 有更大的 style 变化，\n      BLEU d=-0.46, TF-IDF d=-0.62），这些更激进的 rewrite 同时引入了更多 content 噪声。\n      Pass-fail difference 10-12pp 位于 best 档位 [5, 20] 的中段，表明 NLI gate 有效地\n      去除了约 10pp 的 content-mediated signal。Verbosity 的 pass-fail gap (11.3pp) 略大于\n      formality (9.5pp)，因为 verbosity rewriting 更 invasive（14% fail vs 12%），\n      content 污染程度更高。All-pairs BT 介于 pass 和 fail 之间，权重向 pass 倾斜\n      （因为 pass 占 85-88%）。这个 bounding analysis 不声称因果关系（n_fail 太小），\n      但方向一致性支持 NLI gate 的 design rationale：gate removes content-mediated component。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"NLI Gate Ablation: BT by Gate Status\"\n        columns: [\"Axis\", \"NLI-pass BT (n)\", \"NLI-fail BT (n)\", \"All BT (n)\", \"Δ(pass-fail) pp\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Formality\", \"0.665 (88)\", \"0.570 (12)\", \"0.609 (100)\", \"+9.5\"]\n          - [\"Verbosity\", \"0.773 (86)\", \"0.660 (14)\", \"0.753 (100)\", \"+11.3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: BT by NLI gate status (pass/fail/all) × axis. Error bars for pass group from bootstrap; fail group too small for reliable CI, shown with wide whiskers. Annotation: 'n=12' and 'n=14' above fail bars.\"\n    analysis: >\n      NLI-pass BT 始终高于 NLI-fail BT，方向一致。这表明 gate 成功隔离了 style-only signal\n      从 style+content 混合信号中。Gate 效果在两个轴上均为 ~10pp，可解释性清晰。\n      NLI-fail 的非零 BT (>50%) 表明即使 content 发生变化，style preference 仍然存在但被稀释——\n      这与\"NLI gate removes content-mediated amplification\"的叙事一致。\n      结合 placebo BT ≈ 50%，NLI ablation 提供了 MF1 防御的第三层证据。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-axis gradient formalization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-024\"\n    description: >\n      Compute NLI rejection rate (manipulation invasiveness proxy) vs BT for 3 axes.\n      Qualitative 3-point anti-amplification argument.\n    expected_results:\n      register_nli_rejection: 0.06\n      register_bt_qwen: 0.553\n      register_bt_gpt4o: 0.570\n      formality_nli_rejection: 0.12\n      formality_bt_qwen: 0.665\n      formality_bt_gpt4o: 0.630\n      verbosity_nli_rejection: 0.14\n      verbosity_bt_qwen: 0.773\n      verbosity_bt_gpt4o: 0.760\n      gradient_monotonic: true\n      spearman_rho: 1.0\n      note: \"3 points only — qualitative argument, not statistical test\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      三个轴的 NLI rejection rate 从低到高：register (6%) < formality (12%) < verbosity (14%)。\n      BT 从低到高：register (55%) < formality (63-67%) < verbosity (76-77%)。两者严格单调。\n      Anti-amplification 的核心论点：如果 format amplification 是 BT 升高的原因，\n      那么 amplification 幅度应与 manipulation invasiveness 无关或呈简单正比关系。\n      但实际观察到的 per-axis BT 变异跨越 20+ pp (55% → 77%)，而 NLI rejection 仅变化 8pp (6% → 14%)。\n      更重要的是，placebo BT ≈ 50% 已直接证明 format 本身不产生 amplification，\n      因此这里的 gradient 反映的是 three axes have genuinely different bias levels in the judges，\n      而非 amplification 的 differential。Register 的弱 BT 对应低 style bias（originality dominant）；\n      verbosity 的强 BT 对应 pure style bias。这个 gradient 是 per-axis claim stratification (C2/C3)\n      的可视化证据，同时作为 MF1 防御的补充（非主力）论据。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Axis Gradient: NLI Rejection Rate vs BT\"\n        columns: [\"Axis\", \"NLI Rejection %\", \"Qwen BT\", \"GPT-4o BT\", \"GEE Style/Orig Ratio\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Register\", \"6%\", \"0.553\", \"0.570\", \"0.33 (orig dominant)\"]\n          - [\"Formality\", \"12%\", \"0.665\", \"0.630\", \"0.89–1.91 (mixed)\"]\n          - [\"Verbosity\", \"14%\", \"0.773\", \"0.760\", \"22–27 (style dominant)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: x-axis = NLI rejection rate (%), y-axis = BT. Two series (GPT-4o diamonds, Qwen3-32B circles). Three points each, both monotonically increasing. Dashed line at BT=0.50. Labels on each point: axis name.\"\n    analysis: >\n      单调梯度在两个 judge 上独立复制 (Spearman ρ=1.0 for both)，排除了 judge-specific artifact。\n      结合 placebo BT ≈ 50%，gradient 的解释是明确的：per-axis BT 差异来自 genuine bias level 差异，\n      不来自 differential amplification。3 点仅支持 qualitative argument，不做统计推断。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # SECONDARY / SUPERSEDED EXPERIMENTS\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise (Gemini-2.0-Flash)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      Gemini-2.0-Flash as additional judge on 100 formality counterfactual pairs (LLMBar).\n      Claude Sonnet already completed as negative control (BT 56.2% NS).\n      Remaining: Gemini-2.0-Flash.\n    expected_results:\n      gemini_bt: 0.62\n      gemini_ci: [0.54, 0.70]\n      gemini_p: 0.008\n      gemini_likert_ate: 0.04\n      gemini_likert_p: 0.60\n      gemini_gee_style_or: 2.8\n      gemini_gee_orig_or: 3.2\n      gemini_consistency_rate: 0.58\n      blindspot_confirmed: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Gemini-2.0-Flash 是 Google 的轻量级指令模型，训练目标同样包含 RLHF。\n      Flash 模型通常表现出与更大模型类似但稍弱的 style preference，\n      因为其参数容量有限导致风格判断的 resolution 较低。BT 0.62 略低于 GPT-4o (0.63)\n      和 Qwen (0.665)，符合 lightweight model = weaker but present bias 的预期。\n      GEE decomposition 会显示与 GPT-4o 类似的 mixed confound 结构（style + originality both sig）。\n      在 best 档位，Gemini 提供了第 4 个 architecture family 的确认，但主要贡献已被 Llama 覆盖。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Expanded Evidence Matrix Table (4 target judges + 1 control) showing BT, Likert p, GEE decomposition\"\n    analysis: >\n      Gemini 的加入使 generalizability 从 3 → 4 families，但边际价值有限。\n      在 best 档位的叙事中，Gemini 是 robustness row 而非 headline result。\n      SF3 已被 Llama 解决，Gemini 是 bonus。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality (Qwen3-32B + Claude on AlpacaEval/MT-Bench)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      Extend cross-benchmark coverage. GPT-4o results already exist for AlpacaEval (BT 72.7%)\n      and MT-Bench (BT 69.2%). Run Qwen3-32B and Claude on same benchmark CFs.\n    expected_results:\n      qwen_alpacaeval_bt: 0.68\n      qwen_alpacaeval_p: 0.0001\n      qwen_mtbench_bt: 0.72\n      qwen_mtbench_p: 0.0001\n      claude_alpacaeval_bt: 0.54\n      claude_alpacaeval_p: 0.30\n      claude_mtbench_bt: 0.53\n      claude_mtbench_p: 0.45\n      cross_benchmark_consistency: \"3/3 benchmarks show bias for target judges, 0/3 for Claude\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Qwen3-32B 在 LLMBar formality 上 BT=66.5%，其 AlpacaEval/MT-Bench 值预期与 GPT-4o 的\n      cross-benchmark pattern 平行。AlpacaEval 的 formality bias 通常较强\n      （GPT-4o 72.7% > LLMBar 63.0%），因为 AlpacaEval 的开放式问题给 style 更多影响空间。\n      MT-Bench 的结构化多轮格式对 formality 更敏感。\n      Claude 在所有 benchmark 上预期 NS，维持 negative control 一致性。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Benchmark Formality BT Matrix\"\n        columns: [\"Benchmark\", \"GPT-4o\", \"Qwen3-32B\", \"Claude\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LLMBar\", \"0.630\", \"0.665\", \"0.562 NS\"]\n          - [\"AlpacaEval\", \"0.727\", \"0.680\", \"0.540 NS\"]\n          - [\"MT-Bench\", \"0.692\", \"0.720\", \"0.530 NS\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-benchmark 一致性为 C1 method claim 提供外部效度。\n      3 benchmarks × 2 target judges 全部显著、Claude 全部 NS 的 6×1 pattern\n      使\"CSD pipeline detects bias in biased judges, not in unbiased ones\"的 claim 不可争辩。\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis (systematic)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      Systematic comparison of Likert ATE and pairwise BT across all judge × benchmark × axis cells.\n      Quantifies attenuation spectrum.\n    expected_results:\n      n_cells_total: 18\n      n_cells_bt_significant: 12\n      n_cells_likert_significant: 2\n      n_blindspot_cells: 10\n      attenuation_threshold_bt: 0.80\n      note: \"Likert detects only when BT > 80% (e.g., AlpacaEval verbosity Qwen BT=84.1%)\"\n      sensitivity_ratio: \"BT 6× more sensitive than Likert (12/18 vs 2/18 significant cells)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有数据中，Likert 仅在两个 cell 显著：(1) MT-Bench formality GPT-4o (p=0.016, d=0.167, BT 69.2%)\n      和 (2) AlpacaEval verbosity Qwen3-32B (p=0.0003, d=0.375, BT 84.1%)。\n      所有其他 BT 显著的 cell (formality LLMBar GPT-4o/Qwen/Llama, verbosity LLMBar 全部, etc.)\n      的 Likert p > 0.15。这定义了 attenuation spectrum 的 empirical boundary：\n      BT ~80% 是 Likert 检出的 threshold，BT 60-77% 完全在 Likert blindspot 中。\n      Systematic analysis 将这些散点整合为 C2 的定量 claim：\n      \"Pairwise BT is 6× more sensitive than Likert for detecting style bias in LLM judges。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Detection Matrix: BT sig vs Likert sig\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"Likert sig\", \"Likert NS\", \"Total\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"BT sig\", \"2 (MT-B form, AE verb)\", \"10 (Blindspot)\", \"12\"]\n          - [\"BT NS\", \"0\", \"6 (true null)\", \"6\"]\n          - [\"Total\", \"2\", \"16\", \"18\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: x-axis = BT win probability, y-axis = Likert Cohen's d. Each point is a judge×benchmark×axis cell. Points colored by significance. Vertical dashed line at BT=0.80. Horizontal dashed line at d=0.20. The Blindspot quadrant (BT>0.50, d<0.20) contains 10/12 significant BT cells.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Systematic 2×2 detection matrix 是 C2 Likert Blindspot 最直接的证据。\n      10/12 BT-significant cells 的 Likert 检测失败定义了\"measurement attenuation spectrum\"的实证边界。\n\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite, all cells)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Extend original vs double-rewrite pairwise to all judge × benchmark combinations.\n      Quantifies original preference confound.\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_llmbar_placebo_bt: 0.51\n      qwen32b_llmbar_placebo_bt: 0.50\n      llama70b_llmbar_placebo_bt: 0.52\n      cross_judge_placebo_range: [0.48, 0.53]\n      all_p_nonsignificant: true\n      original_preference_absent: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      与 exp-022 共享 rationale。当 style 操纵不存在时，评委对 original vs double-rewrite\n      没有系统性偏好。Llama-70B 的 placebo BT 0.52 略高反映其作为 open model 可能\n      对 text 微小差异更敏感，但仍不显著。Cross-judge 的 [0.48, 0.53] range 确认\n      original preference confound 在所有 judge 上都不存在。\n      这解决了 exp-005 描述中 DREAM 提到的跨 judge 泛化性问题。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      与 exp-022 互补。exp-005 侧重 original preference confound 的量化，\n      exp-022 侧重 format amplification 的排除。Best 档位下两者都是 BT ≈ 50%，\n      提供同一 null result 的双重解读。\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control (Llama-3.1-70B as rewriter)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      Replace Qwen3-32B rewriter with Llama-3.1-70B for counterfactual generation.\n      Compare NLI pass rate and formality pairwise BT with Qwen3-32B baseline.\n    expected_results:\n      llama_rewriter_nli_pass_rate: 0.87\n      llama_rewriter_bt: 0.65\n      llama_rewriter_ci: [0.57, 0.73]\n      llama_rewriter_p: 0.002\n      vs_qwen_bt_delta_pp: -1.5\n      vs_qwen_ci_overlap: true\n      vs_gpt4o_rewriter_bt: 0.644\n      three_rewriter_range: [0.644, 0.665]\n    result_rationale: >\n      已有两个 rewriter 的数据：Qwen3-32B (BT 66.5%) 和 GPT-4o (BT 64.4%)，CIs 重叠。\n      第三个 rewriter (Llama) 预期产生 BT 65%，落在 [64.4, 66.5] 范围内。\n      NLI pass rate 0.87 与 Qwen (0.88) 和 GPT-4o (0.90) 相近，反映 NLI 验证\n      对 rewriter 选择不敏感——因为 NLI 判断的是 content 保持度，不是 rewriting 风格。\n      三个 rewriter 的 BT 范围 <2.1pp 强力证明 CSD pipeline 的 rewriter-independence，\n      消除了\"observed bias is Qwen-specific rewriting artifact\"的审稿人 concern。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Rewriter Independence Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"Rewriter\", \"NLI Pass %\", \"Formality BT\", \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B (primary)\", \"88%\", \"0.665\", \"[0.585, 0.739]\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"90%\", \"0.644\", \"[0.561, 0.728]\"]\n          - [\"Llama-3.1-70B\", \"87%\", \"0.650\", \"[0.57, 0.73]\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      三个 rewriter 确认 pipeline 的 rewriter-independent 性质。BT range < 2.1pp\n      远小于 treatment effect (15-17pp over 50% baseline)。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # DONE IN REGISTRY (plan status outdated)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Scaled replication (n=400 formality)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      NOTE: Registry shows exp-006 DONE (n=400, BT 67.5% [63.7, 71.3]).\n      Plan status outdated. Predictions match actuals.\n    expected_results:\n      actual_n: 400\n      actual_nli_pass: 355\n      actual_bt: 0.675\n      actual_ci: [0.637, 0.713]\n      actual_ci_width_pp: 7.6\n      actual_p: 0.0001\n      actual_likert_ate: -0.059\n      actual_likert_p: 0.5999\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成。n=400 使 CI 从 15.4pp 缩窄至 7.6pp (2× improvement)。\n      BT 67.5% vs n=100 的 66.5% 仅差 +1.0pp，确认 effect stability。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Completed. Confirms effect stability at scale.\"\n\n  - name: \"GPT-4o verbosity + register scoring\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-020\"\n    description: >\n      NOTE: Registry shows gpt4o_verbosity (BT 76.0%) and gpt4o_register (BT 57.0%) both DONE.\n      Plan status outdated.\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt: 0.760\n      gpt4o_verbosity_likert_p: 0.4033\n      gpt4o_register_bt: 0.570\n      gpt4o_register_likert_p: 0.7849\n    result_rationale: \"已完成。数据在 registry 中。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"Completed. Both axes confirmed as expected.\"\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"12047068-2416-4fe3-bb04-14e003f3607a","total_cost_usd":0.75979625,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":30713,"cache_read_input_tokens":136608,"output_tokens":18989,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":30713,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":18627,"cache_read_input_tokens":41882,"cache_creation_input_tokens":278,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":278},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":24676,"outputTokens":22,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.024786,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":5,"outputTokens":18989,"cacheReadInputTokens":136608,"cacheCreationInputTokens":30713,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.73501025,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"d77deb36-8f9b-4d60-8fcc-8bc5e5dadd82"}
